__MACOSX/

# Espalier-Harness runtime — generated, never committed
# Anchored (DEF-429): a bare `reports/` also excludes any nested directory of
# that name. The sibling `.espalier-state/` below stays unanchored on purpose —
# that name is ours, cannot collide, and a hook whose root mis-resolves should
# still get its state ignored. Same rule as cli.py::REQUIRED_GITIGNORE.
/reports/
cc/blueprints/
cc/BLUEPRINT_HANDOFF.md
cc/SURFACE_HANDOFF.md
cc/execution_plan.json
cc/execution_plan.json.lock
# The plan records `execution_plan.py reset` demotes (cc/_cold/<stamp>-execution_plan.json).
# Same line as init's REQUIRED_GITIGNORE entry; without it every reset the session banner
# prescribed left a `??` here and scripts/proof_tier.py refused to run (DEF-788).
cc/_cold/
cc/finding_ledger.jsonl
# Local goal/progress snapshot (curated; refreshed at /handoff, read at SessionStart)
cc/GOAL.md
docs/session-archive.md
docs/blueprint-archive/
.espalier-state/
# TP-49 M1: write_manifest flock sentinel. Per-process lock file, never
# a release artifact.
.espalier/.manifest.write.lock
# TP-150 G-2: freshness manifest read-modify-write flock sentinel. Same
# per-process, never-an-artifact shape as the integrity manifest lock.
.espalier/.freshness.write.lock
# TP-436: fan-out dedup-corpus read-modify-write flock sentinel. Same
# never-an-artifact shape as the two above, but a SIBLING of whatever corpus
# is being written rather than a repo-root path -- append_findings_to_corpus
# takes an arbitrary corpus path (per-round report AND shared corpus), so the
# sentinel is keyed to the file instead of the repo. Matches at any depth, and
# keys on the `.write.lock` suffix the two rows above already use rather than
# on the corpus's extension -- an extension-keyed pattern silently stops
# covering the moment a corpus is not named `*.md`.
.*.write.lock
# Derived freshness state_cache, relocated off the tracked tree so a
# `freshness check` never dirties the working tree. Per-install read-perf
# cache regenerated by any `freshness check`; never a release artifact.
.espalier/.freshness_state_cache.json
# TP-53: per-checkout integrity manifest. Regenerated by
# ``espalier integrity refresh`` on each install; tracking it created
# spurious commit-noise diffs after every refresh and gave the false
# impression that the committed manifest was the "expected" baseline.
# CI runs refresh then verify against the freshly-rendered manifest.
.espalier/integrity.json
# TP-63: reasoning-review aggregate disposition log. Per-operator
# rolling history; not a release artifact.
.espalier/reasoning_review_log.jsonl
# TP-188: memory-promotion disposition log (/reflect candidate pass).
# Per-operator rolling history; not a release artifact.
.espalier/memory_candidate_log.jsonl

# Local-machine Claude Code settings (never committed — settings.json
# records the bare interpreter NAME `espalier init` detected on this
# machine's PATH, so it is machine-specific)
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/settings.json
# TP-171 §5 #1: `espalier init` re-render writes a per-machine settings.json.new
# template for the operator to diff; it carries this machine's detected
# interpreter name and must never be staged/committed.
.claude/*.new
# B-1: `espalier merge-settings` writes a settings.json.bak backup (same
# per-machine content); never commit it either -- nor the numbered
# .bak.1/.bak.2 siblings merge and --rewire-interpreter fall back to,
# which `.claude/*.bak` does not match.
.claude/*.bak
.claude/*.bak.*

# Workspace local artifacts
Finished Tasks/
zDone/
receiver-test/

# Task packs. A `TP-*.md` anywhere is a local working note EXCEPT in the two
# shipped locations (2026-09-21): the forward ledger, its probes file, the
# router and the packs directly under task-packs/ and task-packs/Deferred/ are
# tracked and ship in the source archive. The landed, merged and scrapped packs
# and the dated archive files stay untracked (they live on the record branch).
# Parity twins: .gitattributes (export-ignore per subtree and family -- git
# offers no re-include for a pruned directory, so that wall is a deny-list)
# and surface_contract's `task-packs/` local-only prefix with its
# SHIPPED_TASK_PACK_FILES / is_shipped_pack carve-out.
TP-*.md
TP-*/
*_task_pack.md
# ALLOW-LIST SHAPE, deliberately fail-closed: everything under task-packs/ is
# ignored, then exactly the ship set is re-included, so a new file dropped
# beside the packs (a spec, a scratch note, a findings JSON, a dated archive)
# stays untracked until someone names it here. The directory-content form
# (task-packs/*) is required so the negations can re-include; `task-packs/` as
# a directory exclusion would override every later re-include. Deferred/ is
# re-included as a DIRECTORY first, then its contents excluded, then its packs
# re-included -- git cannot re-include a file whose parent is excluded.
task-packs/*
!task-packs/CLAUDE.md
!task-packs/FORWARD_LEDGER.md
!task-packs/LEDGER_PROBES.json
!task-packs/TP-*.md
!task-packs/Deferred/
task-packs/Deferred/*
!task-packs/Deferred/TP-*.md

# Local orchestrator/blueprint drop-ins (downloaded working notes)
ESPALIER-ORCHESTRATOR-BLUEPRINT*.md

# Local research/blueprint working notes (e.g. failure-mode catalog,
# literature review) — kept in the working tree, not committed.
espalier_*.md

# Ad-hoc fan-out review harnesses (Workflow .mjs scripts) + their findings/report
# outputs — cited as method-of-record in blueprint.md but kept local, same policy
# as the working notes above (no .mjs / _-prefixed review files are tracked).
cc/_pack_review_*
cc/_recall_engine_review*
# live working-summary doc (cc/_ local-only routing excludes it from the
# release archive but NOT from git; per-machine disposable, overwritten at every
# boundary — compaction + handoff — so it must not be committed).
# Live working-summary doc AND its dated per-boundary siblings. The rule was
# `cc/_working_summary.md` alone, which named the live file and not the mirrors
# beside it -- so a dated sibling showed as untracked all session and a `git add -A`
# swept it in (2026-09-01). scripts/record_snapshot.py DISQUALIFIED_PREFIXES already
# refuses this whole prefix as "a rewritten mirror, not the record itself"; the two
# rules now agree on the same population instead of one naming a member and the other
# naming the class.
cc/_working_summary*
# Sidecar to the gitignored cc/GOAL.md. Local session state, made durable through
# refs/heads/record (it is a declared RECORD_ROOT), never through the tracked tree --
# the same treatment as the file it accompanies.
cc/GOAL_OWED.json
# pack-chain driver runtime artifact (the resume ledger). The cc/_ prefix already
# routes it local-only for the release archive; this line is the git-tracking half
# the prefix does not cover (no blanket cc/_*).
cc/_pack_chain_ledger.txt

# pack-chain driver runtime artifact: the committed-but-ungated marker (3-B). Same
# policy as the resume ledger above -- a re-invoke re-gates a pack whose commit landed
# but whose post-commit gates did not finish. Local-only; no blanket cc/_* ignore.
cc/_pack_chain_committed.txt

# pack-chain driver runtime artifact: the pack receipt (cc/_ prefix is local_only
# but there is no blanket cc/_* ignore, so the explicit line is required). The
# red-team repro pair (cc/red_team_{findings,repros}.json) is deliberately NOT
# ignored -- a manual convergence pass commits those as evidence (docs/CONVENTIONS.md
# "Red-team repro contract"); the driver merely clears them with rm -f each pack.
cc/_pack_receipt.json

# Benchmark timestamped artifacts (canonical bench/RESULTS.md is committed)
bench/results/
bench/end_to_end/runs/
# the PowerShell guard rehearsal writes its receipt here; a stray copy has
# blinded ledger probes the way a leftover build/ does
bench/rehearsal-results.json
bench/row-probe-results.json

# Internal release planning (TP-SYN-08)
CONSOLIDATED_RELEASE_PLAN.md

# The codename gate's local arm (DEF-708): one regex per line, `#` comments.
# The terms the public repo must not carry are enforced from this file on the
# operator's machine, so a sensitive name never enters the tracked denylist
# (tests/test_no_internal_codenames.py::FORBIDDEN_PATTERNS stays for names
# that are safe to print). Root-anchored, exact: the classifier's
# _LOCAL_ONLY_PATHS entry is its twin, and the gate's own check-ignore row
# reds the moment this line is lost or the file is force-added.
# memory/local-codename-arm.md says how to recreate the file.
/.local-codenames.txt

# Windows install-rehearsal field notes (2026-08-18 walk). Local-only by
# operator decision. NOTE: the original rationale here -- "the findings were
# scoped into a task pack, so nothing durable needs to point here" -- was
# FALSIFIED (2026-09-09): the record has since grown ~1,800 lines of
# undischarged findings. The durable pointer is now
# memory/windows-walk-output-routing.md, and durability itself comes from
# record_snapshot.py's RECORD_ROOTS. Ignoring stays correct for the reason
# spelled out on the next entry: this path classifies `public`.
WINDOWS_FUSE_NOTES.md
# Windows walk 2 (2026-09-09) findings, distilled from the field record above.
# Ignored for the SAME reason, and the reason is load-bearing: .gitignore doubles
# as the release-exclusion boundary and classify_release_path returns `public` for
# this path, so an un-ignored copy would ship field notes to adopters on the next
# `git add -A`. Durability comes from record_snapshot.py's RECORD_ROOTS, not git.
WALK2_FINDINGS.md
# Windows walk 3 (2026-09-14, all legs 0-5 driven): the INSTRUMENT and its
# preflight analysis, mirrored out of the walk worktree, where they were
# untracked and one `git worktree remove` from gone. Same reason as the two
# entries above and it is load-bearing: classify_release_path returns `public`
# for these paths, so an un-ignored copy ships field notes to adopters on the
# next `git add -A`. Durability comes from record_snapshot.py's RECORD_ROOTS.
# BOTH edits are required for each file -- the snapshot test uses a synthetic
# fixture and will not catch a miss (memory/windows-walk-output-routing.md).
WALK3_RUN_SHEET.md
WALK3_BRIEFING.md
WALK3_PREFLIGHT_FINDINGS.md

# TP-RELEASE-11: classes the release classifier rejects
# (*.code-workspace already present above under IDE section)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
docs/* (*).md
cc/discard_snapshots.log
# Record-branch content-exclusion vocabulary (record_snapshot.py). Local by
# design: the file names the strings the record must withhold, so tracking it
# would publish exactly what it exists to keep out.
.espalier/record_exclude_patterns.txt
